[4] Proof-shaped readout
  Necessary condition for a strict counterexample:
    for every polynomial P with P(0)<0 and P(k)>=0 on k=1..13,
    the exact multiplicity distribution must satisfy E[P(X_S)]>=0.
  Thus every negative moment barrier is a rigorous lonely-time proof.
  In this audit, zero-safe rows found: 2.
  They are expected to be AP/GW boundary atoms in the sampled banks.
  Positive rows missed by selected low-barrier family: 0.
  Candidate theorem:
    Multiplicity moment rigidity for LRC14: outside the AP/GW boundary
    atoms, every primitive qdiv>=14 source-core row has a negative
    admissible moment barrier, preferably one of the odd binomial
    barriers or a bounded root barrier.  A counterexample must therefore
    be moment-indistinguishable from AP/GW before packet labels are seen.
